From cf5f763f0ef8a5b4d8bb4163833cba1160c51894 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 22:55:24 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: gcc-sm6115: let Venus switch the vcodec0 GDSC to
 hardware mode

The Venus driver hands the vcodec0 power domain to the hardware with
dev_pm_genpd_set_hwmode() while a session runs. Without HW_CTRL_TRIGGER
that call is not supported, the driver falls back to polling wrapper
registers that never report the core as on, and VIDIOC_STREAMON fails
with -ETIMEDOUT before any frame reaches the firmware.

QCM2290 uses the same GCC block and already sets the flag at the same
register (0x58098).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016AirPAcjr6JyfsKizshE8B
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6115.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6115.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6115.c
index 4c3804701..c5251aff9 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6115.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-sm6115.c
@@ -3218,6 +3218,7 @@ static struct gdsc gcc_vcodec0_gdsc = {
 	.pd = {
 		.name = "gcc_vcodec0",
 	},
+	.flags = HW_CTRL_TRIGGER,
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
 };
 
